1
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:14,780
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:17,490
Five,

3
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,740
four,

4
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:22,870
three,

5
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,800
two,

6
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:28,620
one.

7
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,190
I'm done.

8
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,030
Are you still there?

9
00:02:50,990 --> 00:02:52,030
Yes.

10
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:55,900
When you came back,

11
00:02:56,350 --> 00:02:58,280
did you have something to say to me?

12
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:02,790
I just wanted to thank you

13
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,740
for always being so good to me.

14
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,520
You're not going to throw up, are you?

15
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:31,890
[The Ninth Thread]

16
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:36,000
[Conditioning: Habits Are Hard to Break]

17
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,150
What would you like to eat?

18
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,360
Nothing.

19
00:03:39,829 --> 00:03:40,329
Nothing?

20
00:03:40,329 --> 00:03:41,670
Babe, you're so cute.

21
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:42,940
Stop it!

22
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:43,660
Love you.

23
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,820
Love you, too.

24
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:48,030
Youth is great.

25
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:06,710
Hi, Dawei.

26
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:13,220
You're here to buy food, too?

27
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,800
The owner just said
the chicken leg rice is sold out.

28
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:23,880
It's okay. I can have
the fish fillet today.

29
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,230
Did you...

30
00:04:32,550 --> 00:04:35,640
have a meal with Keke yesterday?

31
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,370
How did you know?

32
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:41,080
She posted a photo of you two.

33
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,159
I didn't know you saw it.

34
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:51,850
Don't you think it's...

35
00:04:53,030 --> 00:04:54,230
a bit inappropriate?

36
00:04:55,970 --> 00:04:57,630
Which part?

37
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,030
It's just that...

38
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,180
you had a date with someone,

39
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:03,620
and then we...

40
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:05,200
Well...

41
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:08,940
Like...

42
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,060
Is that appropriate?

43
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:25,130
Do you remember what happened last night?

44
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:27,250
Last night?

45
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,150
Yes.

46
00:05:29,490 --> 00:05:30,830
I only remember

47
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,700
I got drunk and went home.

48
00:05:33,590 --> 00:05:35,390
I don't remember anything else.

49
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,210
You don't remember?

50
00:05:39,070 --> 00:05:39,850
No.

51
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,700
I still don't get it.

52
00:05:57,130 --> 00:06:00,060
Why would things be awkward
between you and Wu Dawei?

53
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:01,620
What?

54
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,310
Did you have a fight?

55
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:07,040
It's more complicated.

56
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,220
What could be more complicated?

57
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:13,570
It's just that some things happened,

58
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:15,770
and I don't quite understand.

59
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:17,190
It's weird, isn't it?

60
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:18,600
Why would you ask me?

61
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:20,520
What things could I understand

62
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:21,660
better than you?

63
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:24,510
Got it.

64
00:06:24,530 --> 00:06:25,690
Just touch his thread

65
00:06:25,690 --> 00:06:27,070
like you did last time.

66
00:06:27,090 --> 00:06:28,090
Then you'll understand everything.

67
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:30,320
But things only got more complicated

68
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,920
after I touched his thread.

69
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,409
It's so strange.

70
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,770
Aren't you proud of
how much you can drink?

71
00:06:46,110 --> 00:06:47,860
How did you get drunk last time?

72
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,900
You get drunk
when you have things on your mind.

73
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,790
Actually, I wasn't...

74
00:06:52,790 --> 00:06:54,370
It doesn't matter!

75
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:07,270
Hello?

76
00:07:08,290 --> 00:07:09,010
Keke,

77
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,720
what's wrong?

78
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:13,380
Hi, I got the tickets.

79
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,700
Let's discuss our plans

80
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,500
for the special screening.

81
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:20,200
I remember you said
the movie starts around 5 p.m., right?

82
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,030
Yes.

83
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:23,050
But I'm thinking

84
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:25,310
maybe we can grab lunch together

85
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:28,300
and walk around the shopping mall
near the cinema

86
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,960
before going to see the movie.
What do you think?

87
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,790
Just the two of us?

88
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:36,860
Is it inconvenient for you?

89
00:07:38,110 --> 00:07:39,230
No.

90
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,040
No problem.

91
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:43,300
Okay, see you then.

92
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:49,800
[Psychology Department Lab]

93
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,550
Come on!

94
00:07:51,850 --> 00:07:53,290
Want to be the good person, huh?

95
00:07:53,290 --> 00:07:54,920
You're playing hard to get every day.

96
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:56,260
[Psychology Department Lab]

97
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:55,840
Listen,

98
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:56,790
in the end,

99
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,820
you'll be the only one getting hurt!

100
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,230
[Psychology Department Lab]

101
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:03,850
Ms. Chen Rongmei.

102
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,380
Ms. Chen,

103
00:08:05,410 --> 00:08:07,240
as your daughter,

104
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,740
I must warn you.

105
00:08:09,770 --> 00:08:11,370
This is your own problem.

106
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:13,830
Don't shift the blame to others, okay?

107
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:21,400
Keke.

108
00:08:22,350 --> 00:08:24,300
Here are two hot Americanos,

109
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:26,160
and I also got a cake for you.

110
00:08:26,290 --> 00:08:28,570
You can eat it when watching the movie
with your friend.

111
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:30,090
Thanks for the treat.

112
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:30,950
It's nothing.

113
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,240
I'll go with you to get your scooter.

114
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,059
Okay.

115
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:40,030
Are you sure you won't regret it?

116
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:41,909
There's still an hour
before the special screening.

117
00:08:41,909 --> 00:08:43,909
I can tell my friend not to come out.

118
00:08:44,990 --> 00:08:45,990
I won't.

119
00:08:46,010 --> 00:08:47,740
Just watch it with your friend.

120
00:08:50,630 --> 00:08:51,790
Fine.

121
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,290
I figured

122
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:54,750
you probably have someone you like,

123
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:57,550
so it makes sense you can't
watch the movie with me.

124
00:08:57,590 --> 00:08:58,870
Someone I like?

125
00:08:59,150 --> 00:09:00,110
Really?

126
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:04,890
Isn't it Wu Dawei from the police station?

127
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:08,810
You often mention him when we talk,

128
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:12,180
and you get distracted by his messages.

129
00:09:14,670 --> 00:09:15,690
Anyway,

130
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,130
I think he must be

131
00:09:18,150 --> 00:09:20,440
someone special to you.

132
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:25,970
I'm not sure.

133
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,080
I don't know

134
00:09:30,430 --> 00:09:32,760
if I have the right
to be in a relationship.

135
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:36,260
What right do you need?

136
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,330
Besides,

137
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:38,990
you won't know until you try.

138
00:09:39,790 --> 00:09:40,980
Is that so?

139
00:09:42,390 --> 00:09:43,510
Thanks.

140
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:48,940
And I'm sorry.

141
00:09:48,970 --> 00:09:50,650
Hey, don't apologize!

142
00:09:52,110 --> 00:09:55,630
Well, if you want to make up
for the movie...

143
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:58,250
You'll be the first person I call

144
00:09:58,250 --> 00:09:59,830
next time my scooter won't start.

145
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:00,810
No problem.

146
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:02,830
I can fix it as many times as you want.

147
00:10:03,070 --> 00:10:05,360
If you want to have coffee,

148
00:10:05,410 --> 00:10:08,010
you can come, and it's on me.

149
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,370
Okay, thanks.

150
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,340
You don't need to walk with me.

151
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:13,800
I can go there by myself.

152
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:15,370
Bye.

153
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:16,470
Bye.

154
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,690
It's late. Why hasn't he come back?

155
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,830
The movie should've ended a long time ago.

156
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,400
What's going on?

157
00:10:53,370 --> 00:10:54,770
Where did you go?

158
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,410
I just got off the bus.

159
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:59,200
I'm almost at my grandma's place.
What's wrong?

160
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,830
Why didn't you tell me
you were going back?

161
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,500
I was going to ask you
to play games together.

162
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,000
I told you last time

163
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:08,330
that I'd go back to my hometown
for a few days during this long weekend.

164
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:09,720
You weren't listening at all.

165
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,120
When are you coming back?

166
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:12,180
I don't know.

167
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,830
I might stay for a few more days.

168
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:16,370
It depends on my mood.

169
00:11:17,370 --> 00:11:18,160
Dawei

170
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:20,080
probably doesn't want to see me anyway.

171
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,460
Really?

172
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,610
Alright, that's it.

173
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:26,400
[Great City Life Bus, Siaogang Station]

174
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:23,850
Bye.

175
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:36,500
Grandma,

176
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,860
I'm back!

177
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,580
You're back just in time.

178
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:43,560
I just got back from the market.

179
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:46,900
I also bought your favorite
grouper porridge and egg rolls.

180
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:53,290
I'll go to the farmers' association
and share these with them tomorrow.

181
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,650
Why do you look so thin now?

182
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:58,730
Really?

183
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,750
Have you been eating regularly
and getting enough sleep?

184
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:01,790
I have.

185
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:04,280
I've been working a lot of shifts lately,

186
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,830
so I probably look a bit tired.

187
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:08,530
I haven't retired, and I have money.

188
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,890
Why are you working so many shifts?

189
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,210
I'm fine.

190
00:12:12,230 --> 00:12:13,360
I'm more worried about you, Grandma.

191
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,530
You need more rest at this age.

192
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:19,310
Do you know what we're going to do
in a few days?

193
00:12:19,310 --> 00:12:20,400
I do.

194
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,160
That's why I came back.

195
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:31,720
How time flies.

196
00:12:31,970 --> 00:12:35,670
Jiakai will graduate from college
next year.

197
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:38,940
His grades have always been good.

198
00:12:38,970 --> 00:12:40,550
He's a good kid.

199
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:42,510
The neighbors all say

200
00:12:42,530 --> 00:12:45,830
you raised a great son.

201
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:48,180
You can rest assured.

202
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:54,860
Mom, Dad,

203
00:12:56,370 --> 00:12:57,750
I miss you so much.

204
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,250
Lai?

205
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:08,760
Why are you still lingering around here?

206
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:11,320
What do you mean?
I've been working overtime for five days.

207
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:13,320
Alright, thanks for your hard work.

208
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:15,080
I really can't take it.

209
00:13:15,110 --> 00:13:16,320
I'm going to buy food.

210
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:18,410
Laotao Beef Noodles, do you want some?

211
00:13:18,410 --> 00:13:19,530
Count me in.

212
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,920
Okay, one for you. Dawei, how about you?

213
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,940
Sure, I want
the half-tendon, half-beef noodles.

214
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,150
Two bowls!

215
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,180
One for Jiakai.

216
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,490
Jiakai isn't here.

217
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:27,830
Just one?

218
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,410
Oh, okay.

219
00:13:35,370 --> 00:13:37,120
He's only been back south for one day,

220
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:39,050
and you already miss him that much?

221
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,820
I don't know
what you're talking about, Senior.

222
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:45,120
I've been in a long-distance relationship
for two years.

223
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,810
Do you want some advice?

224
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,870
Is this a trap?

225
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:51,640
Oh, so you know.

226
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:52,900
Jump in.

227
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,360
Jump, jump, jump!

228
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:55,370
Jump, jump!

229
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:57,950
-Jump in with me!
-Senior, you're freaking me out.

230
00:13:57,950 --> 00:14:00,470
Jump, just jump with me!

231
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:14,900
I'm so sorry!

232
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:16,920
I just saw your call.

233
00:14:16,950 --> 00:14:18,700
You also sent a message, right?

234
00:14:19,490 --> 00:14:20,520
It's okay.

235
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:22,920
Have you been busy?

236
00:14:23,650 --> 00:14:25,620
We went to the cemetery this morning.

237
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:28,250
After that, Grandma kept
ordering me around to do chores.

238
00:14:28,250 --> 00:14:30,660
She asked me to sweep the floor,

239
00:14:30,690 --> 00:14:33,500
fix the bike, clean the toilet...

240
00:14:33,650 --> 00:14:34,490
Anyway,

241
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,900
she's got a ton of things for me to do.

242
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:39,780
Sounds like your trip home

243
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:42,010
is busier than working three jobs here.

244
00:14:43,770 --> 00:14:47,770
Yes, Grandma is a master
at bossing people around.

245
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,220
So...

246
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:59,410
Why did you call?

247
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:01,800
Dawei, about that last case...

248
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,380
Are you talking about business?

249
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:04,080
Yes.

250
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:05,310
I'm looking for someone to fix the pipes.

251
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:06,260
Fix the pipes?

252
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:07,590
What pipes?

253
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:10,060
Do I have to fix the pipes now?

254
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:11,750
Hello? Dawei?

255
00:15:12,190 --> 00:15:13,640
Can you hear me?

256
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,350
Hello?

257
00:15:16,030 --> 00:15:17,960
I was just talking to someone else.

258
00:15:20,050 --> 00:15:22,710
So, how long do you plan
to stay in your hometown?

259
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,730
Maybe another four or five days.

260
00:15:26,070 --> 00:15:27,960
There's a farmers' association market
this weekend,

261
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,770
and I'll help Grandma set up her stall.

262
00:15:29,770 --> 00:15:31,910
She's going to sell homemade jam.

263
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,050
That long?

264
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:35,380
What did you say?

265
00:15:36,730 --> 00:15:37,470
Nothing.

266
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,310
I need to get back to work.

267
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:46,290
Okay, go ahead.

268
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:50,250
Okay, good luck.

269
00:15:50,630 --> 00:15:51,260
Bye.

270
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,300
Thanks for your hard work.

271
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:13,250
Getting off work?

272
00:16:14,650 --> 00:16:15,490
What's wrong?

273
00:16:18,490 --> 00:16:21,080
Well, can you do me a favor?

274
00:16:30,350 --> 00:16:32,350
Grandma, where should I put these?

275
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:34,630
Just arrange them unevenly.

276
00:16:34,650 --> 00:16:37,520
I want customers to see

277
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:40,250
how bright and fresh they are,

278
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:43,480
and they'll think
our products are delicious.

279
00:16:45,570 --> 00:16:47,990
Grandma, long time no see!

280
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:48,910
Hello!

281
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:50,620
Why do you have a cute

282
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,890
little helper today?

283
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:52,840
Your boyfriend?

284
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,790
No, he's my grandson.

285
00:16:55,190 --> 00:16:56,590
Hello, miss.

286
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:59,910
Grandma, Earl Grey apple tea?
I didn't see this last time.

287
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:00,540
Oh, this one?

288
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:01,290
Yes.

289
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:02,320
Then you have to buy it today.

290
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,250
Okay, I'll take it this time.

291
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,730
Actually, I'm here to buy
the Golden Banana Rice,

292
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:06,420
but I don't see any.

293
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,770
Get it from the car.

294
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:12,400
-Hurry up!
-Okay, wait a minute.

295
00:17:12,430 --> 00:17:14,540
Thank you so much.

296
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:16,310
Delicious, right?

297
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,740
Let me help you.

298
00:17:39,690 --> 00:17:41,130
Why are you here?

299
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,580
To see you.

300
00:17:47,990 --> 00:17:49,190
Surprise!

301
00:17:50,190 --> 00:17:51,060
Jiang Chaonan?

302
00:17:51,350 --> 00:17:52,760
Why are you also here?

303
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:56,590
My parents are still mad at me

304
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:58,430
because I almost married Liang Chuqing,

305
00:17:58,430 --> 00:18:00,510
and they took my car.

306
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,340
That's why I hired a taxi driver.

307
00:18:02,390 --> 00:18:04,970
I don't like taking public transportation.

308
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:07,550
There are infectious diseases.

309
00:18:07,710 --> 00:18:09,940
Who's a taxi driver?

310
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,610
You're the valet, okay?

311
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:13,690
Take it.

312
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:15,970
Any problem?

313
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:21,500
So, he borrowed your car,

314
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,120
but why do you get to come too?

315
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,200
I have no shift this weekend,

316
00:18:26,470 --> 00:18:28,270
so I came with Chaonan to see you.

317
00:18:28,890 --> 00:18:29,780
What?

318
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:31,440
You don't want to see me?

319
00:18:32,970 --> 00:18:34,850
-It's not like that!
-Jiakai!

320
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,460
What's taking you so long?

321
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:37,870
Our customer is waiting!

322
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:40,370
Coming! Coming, Grandma!

323
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:41,720
Can you help me?

324
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:42,680
Of course.

325
00:18:43,910 --> 00:18:46,540
Come on. One, two, three.

326
00:18:47,570 --> 00:18:49,030
Let's go. You lead the way.

327
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:53,960
Hello, ma'am.

328
00:18:54,430 --> 00:18:56,210
This Grandma's Handmade Jam
is really good.

329
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:56,910
And if you buy it now...

330
00:18:56,910 --> 00:18:58,480
Whiskey citrus?

331
00:18:58,510 --> 00:18:59,820
That's quite special.

332
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:00,490
Yes.

333
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,500
Then I'll take one jar of apple,

334
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:04,560
and one jar of whiskey citrus.

335
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,000
Okay. Thanks.

336
00:19:08,010 --> 00:19:09,740
Young man, you're so handsome.

337
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:12,310
How old are you?

338
00:19:12,330 --> 00:19:13,790
What do you do for a living?

339
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:17,370
I'm 26 years old. I'm a police officer.

340
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,440
That's great!

341
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,570
My relative's daughter

342
00:19:19,570 --> 00:19:21,610
is also 26 years old.

343
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,840
How about I introduce you to each other?

344
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:25,550
No need. Thanks.

345
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,640
It's no trouble at all.

346
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,200
Look,

347
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:29,710
let's add each other on Line,

348
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,620
and I'll give you her contact info.

349
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:32,390
Come on.

350
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:35,000
Come on, add me.

351
00:19:47,670 --> 00:19:48,580
Auntie,

352
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,750
sorry.

353
00:19:49,770 --> 00:19:51,770
He forgot to bring his phone.

354
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:54,920
Yes, I left it at home. Sorry.

355
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:56,380
What a pity.

356
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,400
How much is this?

357
00:19:57,710 --> 00:19:58,960
500 TWD for two jars.

358
00:19:58,980 --> 00:19:59,900
Okay.

359
00:20:01,150 --> 00:20:01,900
Here.

360
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:03,400
Thanks.

361
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:05,500
-Okay, bye.
-Bye.

362
00:20:07,570 --> 00:20:09,570
Can you help me put it in the basket?

363
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:10,460
Okay.

364
00:20:15,410 --> 00:20:16,290
Come on.

365
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,910
-Have some fruit and drinks.
-Let's take a break.

366
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:22,660
I'll buy some bentos later.

367
00:20:23,970 --> 00:20:24,800
Grandma,

368
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:27,700
I ate too much fresh-cut fruit yesterday,

369
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,850
and my stomach is a bit upset.

370
00:20:30,130 --> 00:20:31,920
I need to go to the bathroom.

371
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:34,370
Save some for me.

372
00:20:34,370 --> 00:20:35,180
Don't think about eating

373
00:20:35,180 --> 00:20:37,060
before you even go to the bathroom.

374
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,400
That's gross!

375
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,750
Chaonan is sloppy

376
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:44,080
when it comes to work,

377
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:46,500
but he's serious about eating and pooping.

378
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,740
I'm sorry.

379
00:20:49,810 --> 00:20:52,310
You drove all the way here to have fun

380
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:56,370
but ended up helping out at my stall.

381
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:57,390
Grandma,

382
00:20:57,510 --> 00:20:59,350
I'm glad I could help.

383
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:01,230
You helped a lot.

384
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:03,410
We've almost sold everything.

385
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:05,450
Jiakai,

386
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:08,630
you can hang out
with your friends this afternoon.

387
00:21:10,890 --> 00:21:12,680
What about you, Grandma?

388
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,000
If you're worried,

389
00:21:15,090 --> 00:21:18,210
one of you can stay to help me.

390
00:21:19,290 --> 00:21:20,420
Okay.

391
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:31,970
You're so ridiculous!

392
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:34,440
How could you sneak away
while I was in the bathroom?

393
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,900
Didn't Grandma say you're the best helper,

394
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,850
and she wanted you to stay the most?

395
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:41,100
Yeah, right.

396
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:43,800
You ditched me on purpose.
Don't try to deny it.

397
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,320
Fine.

398
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:47,990
I left extra food for you.
Eat as much as you want.

399
00:21:47,990 --> 00:21:49,870
Okay? That's it, bye.

400
00:21:58,570 --> 00:22:00,430
Didn't you buy a new backpack?

401
00:22:00,450 --> 00:22:01,850
Why didn't you change it?

402
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:05,250
Because after I bought that new bag,

403
00:22:05,250 --> 00:22:08,370
I found it didn't have enough space.

404
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,580
The one you bought seems more suitable.

405
00:22:12,650 --> 00:22:13,700
It's in the back.

406
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:14,620
Take it.

407
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:17,760
Have you been carrying it all along?

408
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,640
Is this for me?

409
00:22:30,870 --> 00:22:32,110
What do you think?

410
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:02,830
Little boy,

411
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:05,330
do you know you violated
the Social Order Maintenance Act

412
00:23:05,330 --> 00:23:07,120
and the Waste Disposal Act?

413
00:23:07,230 --> 00:23:08,440
What did he do?

414
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:10,830
He exposed himself in public and...

415
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:13,180
urinated everywhere!

416
00:23:13,210 --> 00:23:14,050
It ran dry.

417
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:15,830
Stop it!

418
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:19,500
You evil pineapple!

419
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,900
What pineapple?

420
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:25,450
Let me take a picture of you.

421
00:23:26,230 --> 00:23:27,270
Okay.

422
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:32,280
Three, two,

423
00:23:32,310 --> 00:23:33,260
one.

424
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:40,560
I can't remember the last time I went out

425
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,960
and had fun like this during a holiday.

426
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:45,290
You sound like a seasoned soul.

427
00:23:45,290 --> 00:23:47,220
Where's all your youthful energy?

428
00:23:47,230 --> 00:23:49,340
The day Heart‑Stealing Phantom Thief
hits cinemas,

429
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:50,600
I'll drag you to see it,

430
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:53,820
so you can feel the passion!

431
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:55,610
The movie version?

432
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:57,930
Didn't you see it with Keke?

433
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:02,860
We didn't go in the end.

434
00:24:03,370 --> 00:24:04,210
Why?

435
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,750
I gave my ticket to a bigger fan.

436
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,960
Forget about it.

437
00:24:14,230 --> 00:24:16,090
Do you want to see it with me or not?

438
00:24:17,540 --> 00:24:18,410
Sure.

439
00:24:18,910 --> 00:24:20,170
Let's see it together.

440
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:22,030
Then I'll buy the tickets.

441
00:24:22,030 --> 00:24:23,450
Okay, no problem.

442
00:24:33,470 --> 00:24:34,600
Is it Chaonan again?

443
00:24:35,870 --> 00:24:36,680
No.

444
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,680
It's the landlord.

445
00:24:39,340 --> 00:24:42,790
He said the renovation is going smoothly,

446
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:45,690
and we should be able to
move back in two weeks.

447
00:24:54,390 --> 00:24:55,650
Why do you have to move?

448
00:25:24,980 --> 00:25:25,630
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

449
00:25:25,250 --> 00:25:26,500
This is Two-Minute Love Live Stream.

450
00:25:25,630 --> 00:25:26,570
[Two-Minute Love Live Stream]

451
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,660
It's fleeting, so don't miss it.

452
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:29,910
I'm Ms. Peggy.

453
00:25:29,910 --> 00:25:30,370
Today,

454
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:31,500
I'm going to

455
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:32,440
talk about

456
00:25:32,470 --> 00:25:33,580
conditioning,

457
00:25:33,580 --> 00:25:34,690
because it often occurs

458
00:25:34,690 --> 00:25:36,370
in our daily lives.

459
00:25:36,370 --> 00:25:37,270
So, what is it?

460
00:25:37,290 --> 00:25:38,250
There are two types of conditioning.

461
00:25:38,250 --> 00:25:38,960
The first type

462
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:39,960
is called

463
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:42,080
classical conditioning,

464
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:42,540
such as

465
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:45,630
the reaction an animal has
to a specific stimulus.

466
00:25:45,650 --> 00:25:46,990
The most classic example is that

467
00:25:46,990 --> 00:25:48,100
when a bell rings,

468
00:25:48,130 --> 00:25:49,450
a dog hears it and thinks,

469
00:25:49,450 --> 00:25:50,370
"It's time to eat."

470
00:25:50,370 --> 00:25:53,200
Then it'll start salivating.

471
00:25:53,200 --> 00:25:54,100
The second type

472
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:56,200
is called

473
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,870
operant conditioning.

474
00:25:57,870 --> 00:25:58,550
It means

475
00:25:58,570 --> 00:26:00,950
when our voluntary behaviors

476
00:26:00,950 --> 00:26:04,000
result in a reward or punishment,

477
00:26:01,290 --> 00:26:03,790
[Reward or Punishment]

478
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:06,290
[These Stimuli Will Change]

479
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,790
these stimuli will change

480
00:26:05,790 --> 00:26:07,200
or even control our behaviors.

481
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:07,070
[Or Control Our Behaviors]

482
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:07,970
For example,

483
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,370
do you play mobile games?

484
00:26:09,370 --> 00:26:11,870
If you log in consecutively
for a few days,

485
00:26:11,870 --> 00:26:12,750
you can get

486
00:26:12,770 --> 00:26:14,370
a lot of gems or coins.

487
00:26:14,370 --> 00:26:15,590
This is a kind of

488
00:26:15,610 --> 00:26:17,330
operant conditioning.

489
00:26:17,330 --> 00:26:19,500
In romantic relationships,

490
00:26:19,500 --> 00:26:21,000
we often see this happening.

491
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,000
You receive someone's calls or messages

492
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:25,250
at the same time every day.

493
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:26,510
But one day,

494
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:28,370
there are no messages coming,

495
00:26:28,370 --> 00:26:29,440
so you start to feel

496
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:31,250
that something's wrong.

497
00:26:31,250 --> 00:26:32,030
Or perhaps,

498
00:26:32,060 --> 00:26:32,830
you go on a date

499
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:33,790
with someone

500
00:26:33,810 --> 00:26:35,160
every single weekend.

501
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,130
Suddenly, it gets canceled,

502
00:26:37,150 --> 00:26:38,370
and you'll really look forward to

503
00:26:38,370 --> 00:26:39,620
the next date.

504
00:26:39,620 --> 00:26:41,070
At this time, you are

505
00:26:41,090 --> 00:26:43,370
being conditioned.

506
00:26:43,370 --> 00:26:45,000
A roommate you've lived with for a while

507
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,540
suddenly goes back south for a few days,

508
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:48,580
and I suddenly feel so bored.

509
00:26:48,580 --> 00:26:49,870
Am I being conditioned?

510
00:26:49,870 --> 00:26:50,660
Isn't it obvious?

511
00:26:50,660 --> 00:26:51,990
If you're

512
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:52,860
someone

513
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:54,040
who isn't afraid of loneliness

514
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:54,920
and

515
00:26:54,940 --> 00:26:56,450
enjoys being alone,

516
00:26:56,450 --> 00:26:57,860
and when this roommate is away,

517
00:26:57,860 --> 00:26:59,290
you feel a bit uncomfortable,

518
00:26:59,290 --> 00:26:59,910
maybe

519
00:26:59,940 --> 00:27:01,410
you're being conditioned.

520
00:27:01,410 --> 00:27:02,650
Just enjoy the process

521
00:27:02,650 --> 00:27:03,360
and love.

522
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:05,000
Bye.
